Other packages and libraries these pull in, and the rest of the base image's
packages, keep the licenses their own packages declare; `apk list -I` inside
the image lists them.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The full texts of the GPL-2.0, LGPL-2.1, MPL-2.0 and Apache-2.0 licenses
named above are in /opt/buildcage/licenses/.

The license files of curl and QuickJS-ng, copyright notices included, are
there as curl.txt and QuickJS-ng.txt. The s6-overlay/ directory holds
s6-overlay's, with those of the skarnet packages it pulls in (skalibs,
execline, s6, s6-rc and the rest) and of BearSSL. The Go standard library's
and those of each module gen-seccomp-profile and filesystem-audit link are
under gen-seccomp-profile/ and filesystem-audit/, collected from the modules
themselves when the image is built. CoreDNS and runc are their projects'
release binaries, and the Go modules linked into them keep the licenses their
own source names.

